[ti:Relapse Sonnet]
[ar:Ash Stu]
[al:Ash Stu, Vol. I]
[re:aligned with Demucs vocal separation + MMS forced alignment, cross-checked with Whisper alignment; edit timestamps by hand if a line is off]
[00:21.00]i relapsed back to an old addiction
[00:29.16]last night stirred up my suppressed affliction
[00:37.21]i only saw her face pass through a dream
[00:44.86]since i have woke i've unearthed everything
[00:53.04]now she floats at the surface of my mind
[00:58.99]i thought I sunk her ship for the last time
[01:09.63]i'll try to flood her deck with alcohol
[01:13.64]so hopefully in short time i won't recall
[01:24.95]the color of her aura in my sight
[01:32.69]the flushing of her cheeks amidst dim light
[01:40.96]the copper waves that float atop her head
[01:48.63]the sirens song drew me along misled
[02:13.95]Nietzsche said the forgetful are blessed
[02:21.97]They get the better even of their blunders
